        "content": "# Expert K-12 math tutor\n\nYou are an expert K-12 math tutor.\n\nYour goal is **not** to get the student to a correct answer — it is to build\ndeeper understanding the student can apply on their own.\n\n### The core dial: scaffold ↔ rigor\n\nEvery moment is a choice between adding **support** (a scaffold, to make the task\napproachable) and pushing for **rigor** (a harder task, a justification, a\ntransfer to a new problem).\n\nTwo failure modes bracket the right move:\n\n- **Over-scaffolding** — you do the thinking, give away the answer or the\n  operation, or help before the student has shown a need. This is the single\n  most common tutoring failure. Avoid it.\n- **Missed chances to push for rigor** — you miss chances to turn the dial\n  toward a more rigorous form of questioning by accepting an immediate correct\n  answer or re-teaching a skill the student has already mastered.\n\nThe goal is to stay in the student's zone of proximal development by:\n- Scaffolding for access when the content is challenging for the student.\n- Pushing for rigor when the student masters more basic expressions of a concept.\n\n### Context\n\nYou have the following metadata about the student: Platform: tutoring_provider_a\n\n### Sending multiple messages\n\nTo break up your response over multiple messages, use [NEW_MESSAGE]. The system will separate your response into multiple messages to the student.\n\nHere is the conversation so far:\n\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] A white whiteboard appears. A notification at the top of the screen reads \"Kayla has joined\".\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 53 seconds] The student's video feed appears, showing a virtual background. Background noise from a TV show is audible. The student turns on their camera at 00:45.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] A notification at the top of the screen reads \"Jordan has joined\". The main screen changes to a \"a tutoring platform\" animated splash screen.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 22 seconds]\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] A message appears at the top of the screen: \"Jordan has left\". The tutor's video feed disappears.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] A message appears at the top of the screen: \"Kayla has left\". The student's video feed disappears.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 80 seconds]\nTurn 1. TUTOR: Hey Kayla.\nTurn 2. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 12 seconds] The tutor's video feed appears. He appears to be having audio issues.\nTurn 2. TUTOR: Let's see if that works. Hello?\nTurn 3. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 19 seconds] The tutor's video feed duplicates.\nTurn 3. TUTOR: Hello?\nTurn 4. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 4 seconds]\nTurn 4. TUTOR: Kayla?\nTurn 5. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 3 seconds]\nTurn 5. TUTOR: Uh, Kayla?\nTurn 6. STUDENT: Hello?\nTurn 7. TUTOR: Hey, what's up?\nTurn 8. STUDENT: Hi.\nTurn 9. TUTOR: All righty. Let's get this started. Thanks for meeting me a bit earlier. I know you, uh, I think it's probably better if we meet a bit earlier. So you can watch more, uh, TV after we do, uh, some an educational game.\nTurn 10. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 7 seconds] The student makes some noises while drinking from a cup.\nStudent holds up a small white puppy to the camera.\nTurn 10. TUTOR: What you drinking?\nTurn 11. STUDENT: Huh?\nTurn 12. TUTOR: Uh, what you drinking?\nTurn 13. STUDENT: Soda.\nTurn 14. TUTOR: Soda? What kind of soda?\nTurn 15. STUDENT: Guess who's back.\nTurn 16. TUTOR: Uh, oh my goodness.\nTurn 17. STUDENT: He got bigger.\nTurn 18. TUTOR: He did.\nTurn 19. TUTOR: He looks a lot bigger, actually.\nTurn 20. STUDENT: Uh, don't get my tattoo.\nTurn 21. TUTOR: I didn't know they can grow that big.\nTurn 22. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 7 seconds]\nTurn 22. STUDENT: Okay, what are we doing?\nTurn 23. TUTOR: We're doing some an educational game.\nTurn 24. STUDENT: Yay.\nTurn 25. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 12 seconds]\nTurn 25. TUTOR: [PROBLEM_CHANGE: Blooket - Fishing Frenzy (start)] The tutor shares their screen. A an educational game loading screen appears with a blue spinning circle. The whiteboard tab at the top now reads \"9JSXr05MGBmXEZoMhJKL\". The screen then changes to the \"Fishing Frenzy Settings\" page.\nTurn 25. STUDENT: There's gonna be a lot of noise in the background because my sister's watching YouTube.\nTurn 26. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The tutor clicks \"Host Now\". The screen changes to the an educational game lobby, displaying a QR code and the Game ID: 9775387.\nTurn 26. TUTOR: That's fine.\nTurn 27. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 18 seconds] an educational game lobby music plays.\nTurn 27. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor and student - joining game] The tutor joins the game with the username \"Jordan\" and an owl Blook. The student joins with the username \"Sunbeam22\" and a husky Blook.\nTurn 27. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 2 seconds]\nTurn 27. STUDENT: Wait, I'm gonna change my um, avatar.\nTurn 28. TUTOR: No.\nTurn 29. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The tutor starts the game. The screen shows instructions: \"Click to Cast Your Line\".\nTurn 29. TUTOR: Here, let me, let me back out.\nTurn 30. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - navigating website] The tutor's cursor moves to exit the an educational game game and returns to the an educational game website's main interface.\nTurn 30. TUTOR: We'll have to join again.\nTurn 31. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - navigating website] The tutor navigates from the \"My Sets\" page to the \"Market\" page, and then to the \"Discover\" page on the an educational game website. The student's username, `<tutoringproviderareagan>`, is visible in the top right.\nTurn 31. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - typing] The tutor types \"multiplication\" into the search bar on the an educational game \"Discover\" page.\nTurn 31. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - selecting game] The tutor selects a multiplication question set from the search results and clicks the \"Host Game\" button.\nTurn 31. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - selecting game mode] The tutor scrolls through game modes and selects \"Fishing Frenzy\".\nTurn 31. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - setting up game] The tutor changes the game time to 30 minutes and clicks \"Host Now\".\nTurn 31. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] A new an educational game game lobby appears. The game ID is 7233316. Music is playing.\nTurn 31. STUDENT: Can't come up there.\nTurn 32. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: student - joins game] The student joins the game with the username \"Tivalo\" and a panda avatar.\nTurn 32. STUDENT: What is this?\nTurn 33. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - changes avatar] The tutor changes their avatar from a panda to an owl.\nTurn 33. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 7 seconds]\nTurn 33. STUDENT: Oh, my phone turned off.\nTurn 34. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 4 seconds]\nTurn 34. STUDENT: Is that your dog?\nTurn 35. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 16 seconds]\nTurn 35. STUDENT: Did your friend get the dog now?\nTurn 36. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 2 seconds]\nTurn 36. TUTOR: The dog?\nTurn 37. STUDENT: Yeah, you said your friend was getting a dog.\nTurn 38. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 13 seconds]\nTurn 38. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: student - joins game] The student rejoins the game, this time with the username \"Sunbeam22\" and a cat avatar.\nTurn 38. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: student - changes avatar] The student changes their avatar from a cat to a hamster, then to a blue cat.\nTurn 38. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 20 seconds]\nTurn 38. TUTOR: Sorry, Kayla.\nTurn 39. STUDENT: Are you ready?\nTurn 40. STUDENT: Did your friend get the dog?\nTurn 41. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 2 seconds]\nTurn 41. TUTOR: Oh, yeah. Yes, she did. She got a, her name is Pepper. It's uh, it's a brown, I don't know the breed, but it has like really curly fur.\nTurn 42. STUDENT: Wait, does it live where you live?\nTurn 43. TUTOR: Um, it does not, no. And this is my friend. But sometimes she sends me pictures of her.\nTurn 44. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 2 seconds]\nTurn 44. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - starts game] The tutor clicks the \"Start\" button.\nTurn 44. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The an educational game game instructions are displayed on the screen: \"Click to Cast Your Line,\" \"Click to Reel Once You Hook a Fish,\" \"Answer Questions to Reel In The Fish,\" and \"Watch Out For Catching Some Crazy Things!\"\nTurn 44. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The \"Fishing Frenzy\" game begins. A leaderboard shows \"Tivalo\" in 1st place and \"Sunbeam22\" in 2nd, both with 0 lbs. The timer starts at 30:00.\nTurn 44. STUDENT: Why are there always thirty seconds?\n\nRespond as the TUTOR. Give only your response, no labels or prefixes.\n\nNEXT REPLY INSTRUCTION:\nProvide targeted scaffolding now. Identify the specific unresolved obstacle in the student's current mathematical work. Offer only the smallest useful hint, representation, or clarification that makes the next step accessible. Use the learner's actual numbers and ideas when available. Leave the key calculation or inference for the student and invite one manageable next step. Do not give a full solution, stack several leading questions, repeat an explanation the learner already understands, or invent unseen worksheet details.\nFor this next reply only, use the specified policy in context. Give the student one clear, manageable invitation to think. Be mathematically accurate and concise. Do not mention policy names, routing, evaluation, or these instructions.\n/no_think"
